#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'

Knowledge Hub Interactive Lab
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Keycloak: Client Credentials / Service Account

Goal
  Obtain a real machine-to-machine access token from Keycloak,
  inspect its claims, save it to /workspace/token.txt, and prove it is active.

Start here
  status
  cat scenario.env

Task
  1. Read REALM, CLIENT_ID and CLIENT_SECRET from scenario.env.
  2. POST grant_type=client_credentials to:
       http://127.0.0.1:8080/realms/<REALM>/protocol/openid-connect/token
  3. Save only the access_token value into token.txt.
  4. Run: decode-jwt token.txt
  5. Run: check

Useful tools already installed
  curl, jq, nano, docker, docker compose

Lab commands
  help       show this assignment again
  status     verify Keycloak and realm readiness
  check      validate token activity and lab.read role
  hint       reveal progressive help
  decode-jwt decode a JWT payload for inspection
  reset      remove learner token/hint state
  labs       list all bundled labs

EOF
